      "description": "The servant spirit of the Turkish tales. In The Cinder-Youth, striking a flint-stone kept in a casket summons \"a black efrit with a mouth as big as the world\", who asks \"What dost thou command, my Sultan?\" and fetches meat, water, news and people at once. He is enormous and fearsome, but he serves whoever holds the talisman.",
